# Rust crates

## `crates/git`

- Git CLI runner + parsers + models + services
- Prefer CLI for data; git2 only when you need control over long-running/stateful ops (clone progress, future rebase UI, etc.)
- Keep parsers and domain services here — not in the TS app

## `crates/ipc`

- App/IPC concerns **without** embedding git parse logic
- Repo manager, sessions, clone/init orchestration, persisted store, etc.
- Stay independent so ipc can evolve without dragging git internals

## `crates/logger`

- Small internal logging helper only

Tauri wires both crates from `apps/desktop/src-tauri`. After public command API changes, run `make typegen`.
